  {
    "id": "pepe-essentials",
    "title": "Pepe Essentials",
    "kind": "emote",
    "tagline": "Every feeling, as a frog.",
    "lore": [
      "Pepe the Frog comes from Matt Furie’s comic Boy’s Club (2005), where his line “feels good man” spread across the internet from 2008. Edits of him became one of Twitch chat’s largest emote families, one for nearly every emotion.",
      "His history isn’t all light: from 2015–16 he was misused by the alt-right, and Furie spent years reclaiming the character (the 2020 documentary Feels Good Man tells that story). In 2019 Hong Kong protesters adopted him as a pro-democracy symbol. Today’s chat Pepes are the everyday kind collected here."
    ],
